wikipedia_extract: 'Libeccio was one of four Maestrale-class destroyer built for the
  Regia Marina (Royal Italian Navy) in the early 1930s. Completed in 1934, she served
  in World War II.

  She was present during the Battle of Taranto, and suffered a direct bomb hit, however
  it passed through her hull without exploding. She was also present at the disastrous
  Battle of the Duisburg Convoy, though survived only to be torpedoed the next day
  by HMS Upholder when she returned to the scene to search for survivors, she was
  taken in tow but soon sank.'
